## CORE FEATURES

### 1. The Growth Tracking System™

**What It Tracks:**
```yaml
Metrics:
  - learning_velocity: (skills[today] - skills[yesterday]) / time
  - iteration_count: number of improvement cycles per feature
  - complexity_progression: fibonacci sequence of feature difficulty
  - collaboration_coefficient: knowledge shared * team_impact
  - ai_utilization_efficiency: quality of prompts * iteration on responses
```

**Implementation:**
- GitHub Actions that run on every commit
- Public dashboard (METRICS.md) that auto-updates
- Personal trajectory graphs showing growth over time
- Team velocity comparisons (anonymized)

### 2. AI Assistant Integration (Claude Nodes)

**Components:**
- CLAUDE.md with prompt templates
- Achievement-locked advanced prompts
- Quality scoring for prompts (S.P.E.C. system)
- Prompt iteration tracking

**Key Features:**
- Starter templates for common tasks
- Progressive prompt complexity
- Meta-prompting exercises
- Prompt quality metrics

### 3. The Gamification Layer

**Achievement System:**
```javascript
achievements = {
  "First Blood": "First successful commit",
  "Iteration Champion": "10 improvements on single feature",
  "Prompt Engineer": "S.P.E.C. score > 75",
  "Growth Spurt": "3x velocity increase in one week",
  "The Debugger": "Fix others' code 5 times",
  "Full Stack": "Complete vertical feature slice",
  "The Mentor": "Help 3 teammates level up"
}
```

**Clearance Levels:**
- INFRARED (Week 1-2): Basic syntax, first commits
- RED (Week 3-4): Simple features, debugging
- ORANGE (Week 5-6): Error handling, testing
- YELLOW (Week 7-8): Refactoring, patterns
- GREEN (Week 9-10): Architecture, scaling
- BLUE (Week 11-12): Performance, optimization
- INDIGO (Week 13-14): Teaching others, code review
- VIOLET (Finals): Full stack features

### 4. The Dystopian Wrapper

**Environmental Elements:**
- Daily "Productivity Reports" from The Algorithm™
- "Mandatory Happiness Surveys" (actually reflection prompts)
- "Performance Optimization Meetings" (actually pair programming)
- "Compliance Training" (actually best practices)
- "Algorithm Feedback Sessions" (actually code reviews)

